    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d550">

                <pb facs="0720" n="612" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg612"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic">February 13,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 4th
                    instant, inclosing a copy of the draft of the proposed Behring Sea arbitration
                    convention I have <pb facs="0721" n="613" xml:id="pg613"/> the honor to inform
                    you that, as previously arranged between us, I transmitted a copy of the draft
                    by the mail of the 6th instant to the Marquis of Salisbury for the approval of
                    Her Majesty’s Government, and that I am awaiting his lordship’s instructions
                    before proceeding further in the matter.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
